Priya (CSE): Heads-up — enterprise customer hitting 422 on /v1/rerank. They sent a payload with nested passages inside candidates and a different query field name. Error: "Unrecognized field 'query_text'". Repro below. :face_with_raised_eyebrow:

Tom (Eng): Can you paste the exact curl and error body? Also request_id if available.

Priya (CSE): Sure — request_id: r-27c9f1a8. Error body: `HTTP/1.1 422 Unprocessable Entity
{"error":"Unrecognized field 'query_text' (class java.lang.String), not marked as ignorable"}`

Payload they sent: ```json
{
  "query_text": "Which article best explains our refund policy?",
  "candidates": [
    {
      "id": "doc_123",
      "title": "Refunds and returns",
      "passages": [
        {"text": "You can return within 30 days if...", "offset": 0},
        {"text": "Exceptions: digital goods...", "offset": 240}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "doc_456",
      "title": "Subscription cancellations",
      "passages": [
        {"text": "Cancel anytime from settings...", "offset": 0}
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

Nina (ML Eng): Two quick things: 1) field name — our rerank endpoint expects `query` (string) at the top-level, not `query_text`. 2) shape — rerank accepts either a `candidates` array where each candidate has a top-level `text` string to score, OR a `documents` array where each document contains `passages`. From your payload they mixed both: `candidates` with `passages`. That confuses the server mapping.

Sam (Support): Do we return a different 4xx for the shape mismatch? The error mentions `query_text` specifically which is why they hit 422.

Nina (ML Eng): Right — the JSON parser fails on unknown top-level fields first. If you fix the key to `query` the service will then validate the candidates shape and either accept or return a clearer validation error. We should still tighten error messages for the mixed-case. Filing a follow-up to eng-runtime.

Priya (CSE): Customer asks for minimal patch so they can prod in staging. Suggested quick transform: flatten passages into candidates and rename field. I suggested this curl to test locally: ```bash
curl -s -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/v1/rerank \n  -H 'Authorization: Bearer $KEY' \n  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \n  -d '{"query":"Which article best explains our refund policy?","candidates":[{"id":"doc_123_p0","text":"You can return within 30 days if..."},{"id":"doc_123_p1","text":"Exceptions: digital goods..."},{"id":"doc_456_p0","text":"Cancel anytime from settings..."}]}'
```

Tom (Eng): Good repro. Also note limits — default `max_candidates` is 100 (and there is a hard cap of 1024 depending on model). If they had thousands of passages flattened we could hit 413/429 or memory limits. Ask customer to try small set (<=50) first.

Priya (CSE): They only sent ~18 passages total. So limits shouldn't be the immediate issue. They mainly hit the 422.

Nina (ML Eng): For longer-term: if they want document-level scoring, use `documents` payload: ```json
{
  "query": "...",
  "documents": [
    {"id":"doc_123","passages":[{"text":"..."}]},
    {"id":"doc_456","passages":[{"text":"..."}]}
  ]
}
```
We internally expand documents->passages to candidates, but the API needs the correct top-level key. Also watch `score_normalization` flag — when off you can see unexpected score ranges depending on model variant.

repro-bot: Repro run created: https://repro.redwood.ai/r/1945678901 — linked logs (customer staging payload sanitized).

Sam (Support): I'll reply to customer with the two-step patch (rename `query_text` -> `query`, flatten passages into `candidates[].text`) and ask them to try the curl above. I'll also include short-term workaround and note we're escalating to eng-runtime for clearer error message on mixed `candidates`+`passages`.

Nina (ML Eng): If they still see weird scores after fix, ask for the exact response object (we'll want the unredacted `scores` array + model name). Sometimes model variants return non-normalized logits; we can apply a softmax client-side as a fallback.

Priya (CSE): Thanks — sending patch now. Will update thread when customer validates in staging. :thumbsup:
